Her glass filled with the official result.

TARGET DISTRESS REDUCED
SLEEP CYCLE STABILIZED
AGGRESSIVE RECOGNITION EVENTS RESOLVED
FAMILY STRUCTURE COHERENT
MINOR RESIDUAL CONTRADICTION
BELOW REPORTABLE THRESHOLD

Venn read the final line twice.

The system had already classified the contradiction as minor.

B stood.

His knees felt unreliable.

Simon remained beside the bed.

"What do we tell him?"

B looked at the train, still in Elias's hands.

"Tell him someone is missing."

"Who?"

"I don't know."

Simon looked at him.

Neither of them spoke.

B started toward the door.

"Will the constraint hold?" Simon asked.

"I don't know."

"For how long?"

"I don't know that either."

Simon looked at Elias.

His father was turning the train over in his hands, searching the wood for an answer it could no longer provide.

"If something else happens," Simon said, "can I request you again?"

B looked at him.

"You requested me this time."

Simon did not answer.
